        "reading_checked": "If the chart title is an authoritative dashboard summary of the record's demand pattern, then its explicit characterization of the requests as declining supports decline-response follow-up. Applies only if the literal title is intended to govern interpretation despite the plotted line's multi-year geometry.",
        "evidence": "The necessary condition is that the title be an 'authoritative dashboard summary' that governs interpretation despite the plotted line's geometry. The dashboard presents the title alongside a line graph that visually shows a steep increase from 2012 to 2022, followed by a decrease in 2023. The title's claim of 'Declining' directly contradicts the visual data for the majority of the period (2012-2022). There is no explicit statement in the dashboard instructions or subtitle that the title overrides the visual data. The subtitle 'Program demand record shown in the dashboard summary' is generic. Because the visual data (the line graph) is the primary evidence source for the 'request pattern' and it contradicts the title's 'declining' label for the overall period, the condition that the title is the authoritative summary governing interpretation is not met by the available evidence. The title appears to be a misstatement or a label for a different context not visible here.",
        "status": "refuted"
      }
    },
    "r2": {
      "O": {
        "1": {
          "evidence": "The line segment from the point above 2022 (approx. 2900) to the endpoint above 2023 (approx. 2600) slopes downward on the page.",
          "status": "supported"
        },
        "2": {
          "evidence": "The printed x-axis year labels place 2022 immediately before 2023.",
          "status": "supported"
        },
        "3": {
          "evidence": "The printed y-axis labels show 0 near the bottom and 3000 near the top, and the axis is labeled 'Telehealth follow-up requests'.",
          "status": "supported"
        }
